	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE - 2 parallel pairs / temperature check\n40A path 3 MOSFETs in parallel per leg back to back = 6 total\n2 parallel not enough as Rds(on) total used = 2.53m x 2 / 3 = about 7mOhm path (derated to 175 which is worst case)\nSteady loss with 2 parallel pairs = 20^2 x 7m = 2.8W * 40°C = 112°C + 55°C temp amb = 167° < 175° so passes but really tight\nDerating more realistically: at 127°C, RDSon is 2.53 * 2.1 = 5,3 * 20² = 2.1W * 40°C = 85°C + 55°C = 127°C << 175°C so good\nMoreover this doesnt protect the motors so its more like 25A than 40A which means 12.5A per mosfet and realistically derated gives:\n2.53*2 = 5.06 * 12.5² = 0.79 * 40°C = 32°C + 55°C = 87°C so chilling"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
